## Migration

Before:

```toml
[models]
"kimi-k2.6" = { provider = "fireworks" }

[provider.models]
"kimi-k2.6" = { adapter = "chat" }
```

After:

```toml
[provider.routes]
chat_completions = "chat"
messages = "chat"

[provider.model_aliases]
"kimi-k2.6" = "accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2.6"
```

Client changes from:

```text
POST /v1/chat/completions
```

to:

```text
POST /providers/fireworks/v1/chat/completions
```

The request body keeps the model:

```json
{
  "model": "kimi-k2.6",
  "messages": []
}
```

Temporary compatibility:

```toml
[server]
default_provider = "fireworks"
```

## Deferred Features

These are intentionally outside the initial implementation:

- Header-based provider selection.
- Global model routing or weighted provider selection.
- Automatic discovery during server startup.
- Background scheduled catalog refresh.
- Native upstream token-count APIs.
- Multi-provider merged `/v1/models`.
- Database-backed catalogs.
- Per-client model access control, since the proxy currently has no inbound
  authentication.

